        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dc6ad132-301c-5d97-9da1-e50aa1042e89",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Xinghua, Jiangsu; Taizhou; Yancheng; Yangzhou; Jingdezhen; Jiangxi; Anhui; China\n- People: Hou Yifan; Mariya Muzychuk; Sergey Karjakin; Magnus Carlsen\n- Events: Women's World Chess Championship 2016; Candidates Tournament; World Chess Championship 2016\n- Topics: Chess\n\nFacts:\n- Xinghua is a county-level city under the administration of Taizhou in Jiangsu province, China.\n- Xinghua borders Yancheng to the north and east and Yangzhou to the west.\n- Jingdezhen is a prefecture-level city in northeastern Jiangxi province, China, and it borders Anhui to the north.\n- In 2007, Jingdezhen had a total population of 1,554,000.\n- Hou Yifan was born on 27 February 1994 in Xinghua, Jiangsu, China.\n- Hou Yifan is a Chinese chess grandmaster and former chess prodigy.\n- In 2016, Hou Yifan defeated Mariya Muzychuk in the Women's World Chess Championship 2016.\n- In 2016, Sergey Karjakin won the Candidates Tournament and then challenged Magnus Carlsen in the World Chess Championship 2016.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
